# Upstream documentation snapshot — {{ source_name }}

Source of truth for every endpoint wrapper (ADR-0003). Files in this directory are
fetched from {{ upstream_docs_url }} by `/refresh-upstream`, never edited by hand but
`OBSERVED.md`, where it exists: what upstream does but never documents, each note with
its evidence. They are refreshed deliberately by PR so that changes show up as diffs.
Once `scripts/refresh_upstream.py` is filled, it writes them and regenerates this file
whole.

## Attribution

(The copyright line as the documentation states it, e.g. `© 2026 Example Ltd.`, with
the page that prints it, or "none stated"; where `scripts/refresh_upstream.py` captures
the documentation, it checks this on every run and stops when the documentation starts
to state one or stops printing one.) The documentation's text is reproduced here as this
package's reference (ADR-0003); the publisher's objection is met by replacing it with a
summary that keeps the names and semantics the wrappers rely on.

## Files and pages

`Fetched` is the UTC time of the run in ISO 8601 with an explicit `Z`
(`2026-10-24T09:15:00Z`). Bytes and sha256 are those of the body as fetched, ETag as
sent and Last-Modified in UTC, `-` where none is sent. A table with merged cells
(`rowspan`, `colspan`) or a table nested in it, which a Markdown pipe table cannot hold,
is kept as its HTML in the Markdown file, and its row's note says so. The capture script
writes these kinds of row, here with example values:

- a file, kept verbatim or converted: its path and the page it was made from;
- a page recorded without a file, a 404 or a page without documentation text:
  `(no file)` and its status, and no size, sha256 or ETag where its body changes on
  every request;
- an excerpt, this source's part of a shared document (conventions §3): its path, with
  the whole document's size and sha256;
- a sample, a small answer of the API kept verbatim under `samples/`, which documents the
  answer's shape and is no test fixture: its path and the URL it was requested from;
- `OBSERVED.md`, written by hand, which the script neither writes nor checks.

```text
| openapi/openapi.json | https://api.example.org/openapi.json | 2026-10-24T09:15:00Z | 200 | 48213 | 3f2a…c9e1 | - | 2026-10-20T08:00:00Z | SPEC_URL, verbatim |
| (no file) | https://api.example.org/status | 2026-10-24T09:15:00Z | 404 | - | - | - | 2026-10-20T08:00:00Z | a status page with a per-request reference |
| openapi/part.json | https://api.example.org/shared.json | 2026-10-24T09:15:00Z | 200 | 912044 | 7d0c…5a2f | - | - | excerpt of a shared document; Bytes and sha256 are the whole document's |
| samples/items.json | https://api.example.org/v1/items?limit=2 | 2026-10-24T09:15:00Z | 200 | 412 | 9b1e…04d7 | - | - | a sample: an answer of the API, kept verbatim; no test fixture |
| OBSERVED.md | - | - | - | - | - | - | - | written by hand: what upstream does but never documents; not fetched or checked |
```

