## Not fetched

A page the documentation links that the snapshot deliberately does not request, a feed, a
third-party specification (cited, not snapshotted), an API answer or a page that is no
API documentation, has a row with its reason. A page that an anonymous client cannot read
is requested once, without credentials, and its row gives the status and the host it
redirects to (conventions §3). For example:

```text
| https://api.example.org/feed.xml | (not requested) | - | a feed of releases |
| https://api.example.org/admin | 302 | login.example.org | a login on another host |
```

